  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cosmicstack-labs/mercury-agent/zipball/v1.2.5",
  "body": "The release where **1.2.4's promises actually ship.** The squash merge into main silently dropped the newest Release/1.23 work — the native-scrollback TUI, the flicker fix, the chat delivery contract, and even `mercury attach`'s command registration — so the shipped package had the code but not the features. All of it is restored and verified here.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### Native scrollback — wheel scroll and copy-paste are the terminal's own\n- Finalized messages print **once** into the terminal's native scrollback through `<Static>`; only the small live region (streaming tail, steps, prompt, input, status) repaints\n- **Mouse reporting stays OFF in Mercury Code** — the terminal itself handles wheel scrolling and drag-select/copy-paste; synthetic mouse capture would break both\n- Viewport anchoring keeps the live region pinned while you scroll back freely\n\n### The flicker fix — diff-rendered live region\n- Ink's frame writer is patched (shipped via the ink patch) to **erase and rewrite only the rows that changed**: a permission-selection toggle or a spinner tick no longer repaints the entire live region — no more full-UI flash on every keystroke of state\n\n### Chat delivery contract — no false positives, anywhere\n- The completion contract now holds for plain chat on every channel: an implementation-style request must actually run its tools — narration alone can't end a task without having done anything\n- A change that landed but was never verified is forced through one bounded evidence round (build/test/typecheck), same as execute mode\n- **Text deliverables stay exempt**: poems, emails, essays — replies where the response itself is the work — are never forced through file tools\n\n### `mercury attach` — now actually works\n- 1.2.4 shipped the attach code but **lost the command registration in the merge**; `mercury attach` didn't exist there\n- Full command wiring restored: `mercury attach` connects a second terminal to the running runtime (live streaming TUI), a second `mercury` invocation auto-attaches, and the machine-local attach token rotates at every boot\n- Detach with Ctrl+C — the runtime keeps running\n\n## Fixed\n- Restored Release/1.23 work dropped by a conflicted merge (`40f5aea`): 11 files, including the ink patch's log-update diff-render, the scrollback TUI, the attach wiring, and the chat delivery contract — verified by tree-diff against the feature-complete commit"
}
